Defensive fix: preserve <br> line breaks inside <address> tags in _extract_plaintext_authors

Repo: https://github.com/cppalliance/wg21-paperflow/pull/66
Source: CodeRabbit review comment on commit 121de46

File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/html/extract.py, line 66
Current:  lines = [a.get_text(strip=True) for a in addr_tags if a.get_text(strip=True)]
Fix:      lines = [a.get_text("\n", strip=True) for a in addr_tags if a.get_text(strip=True)]
Then split on "\n" and filter empty lines, same as the non-address branch (line 62).

Why: get_text(strip=True) without a separator collapses <br> into nothing.
If an <address> tag ever contains Name<br>obfuscated_email, the name and
email merge into one string and deobfuscate_email returns the wrong span offset.

Priority: Low. No known WG21 paper triggers this. All real-world obfuscated-email
papers (p2285r1 pattern) use one <address> per author without <br>.
The plaintext fallback only runs when mailto links are absent. Purely defensive.
